Chapter: CtorBoundedProbe
  cites Foreword chapter List

 Does a bounded CONSTRUCTOR payload survive the IR round trip by name?
 IRTypeEmission.md measures zero bounded constructor payloads across all
 six corpus units, on both sides, so that is no evidence either way. The
 record field `pc` is the positive control: its bounds are known to be
 published as `(a-bounded ...)` in type-defs. `Present` carries the same
 band in a constructor payload. If type-defs publishes one and not the
 other, option A cannot recover the sum side by name.

Section: Types

  Reading =
   | Absent
   | Present (Integer between -100 and 100 clamping)

  Elem = record {
   nm : Text,
   rd : Reading,
   pc : Integer between 0 and 100 clamping
  }

Section: Data

  elems : List Elem
  elems = [
   Elem { nm = "e0", rd = Absent, pc = 5 },
   Elem { nm = "e1", rd = Present 7, pc = 50 }
  ]

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
   print-line-uni ("n=" & show (list-length elems))
  end

